# Copy to .env.local for local development, and set the same values in your
# host (Vercel > Settings > Environment Variables) for deployments.
#
# With none of these set the site still runs: the chat widget answers 503 and
# shows its error line, and captured leads are logged server-side instead of
# being filed anywhere. That is enough to click through the flows, but not to
# launch on.

# ---- Chat assistant: Aleesa Web Chat (preferred) --------------------
# Set BOTH and the Aleesa provider takes over from ANTHROPIC_API_KEY below.
# The bot is then trained in the Aleesa dashboard — Knowledge Base plus the
# Chat Agent — so the system prompt in src/lib/chat/anthropic-provider.ts is
# NOT used, and every conversation lands in the Aleesa inbox where a human
# can take over.
#
# Setup, once:
#   1. Aleesa dashboard > Settings > Connections > Web Chat > "Enable Web
#      Chat". That generates the tenant API key; copy it there and then —
#      afterwards only a masked version is shown, and regenerating it
#      invalidates the old key immediately.
#   2. Paste it as ALEESA_WEBCHAT_API_KEY below.
#   3. ALEESA_WEBHOOK_URL is the Aleesa *webhook server* origin, with no
#      trailing path — "/webhooks/web-chat" is appended by the adapter.
#   4. Verify with "Test Web Chat" in the same dashboard card before
#      pointing the site at it.
#
# The key is a server-only secret: it identifies the tenant and anyone holding
# it can post as this site. Never rename it with a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix — it is
# read in src/lib/chat/aleesa-provider.ts, which only ever runs inside the
# /api/chat route handler.
# ALEESA_WEBHOOK_URL=https://webhooks.your-aleesa-host.com
# ALEESA_WEBCHAT_API_KEY=

# ---- Leads -> Aleesa CRM (Website Form intake) ----------------------
# Set BOTH and every captured lead — the enquiry form on /contact, the
# newsletter signup, and the three resource lead magnets on /property,
# /business-ai and /wellness — is filed in Aleesa as a Lead with source
# "website_form", carrying the full submission.
#
# Setup, once:
#   1. Aleesa dashboard > Settings > Connections > Website Form >
#      "Enable Website Form". Copy the key there and then — afterwards only a
#      masked version is shown, and regenerating it invalidates the old key
#      immediately.
#   2. Paste it as ALEESA_WEBSITE_FORM_API_KEY below.
#   3. ALEESA_API_URL is the Aleesa *API* origin — a different host from
#      ALEESA_WEBHOOK_URL above. Either an origin or the full submit URL
#      works: the path "/api/v1/integrations/website-form/submit" is appended
#      by the adapter only when it is not already there.
#
#      Heads up: the dashboard card can print the submit URL against
#      "api-aleesa.ai", which does not resolve. It derives that host from the
#      browser URL when the dashboard's own API base is unset. The host that
#      answers is api.aleesa.ai — hyphen to dot.
#
# Server-only secret, like the web chat key: anyone holding it can file leads
# as this tenant. Never rename it with a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix — it is read in
# src/lib/chat/aleesa-leads.ts, which only runs in the API routes.
#
# Each capture point arrives under its own formId, so they can be told apart
# and automated separately in Aleesa:
#   contact-enquiry               /contact enquiry form
#   newsletter-signup             newsletter band
#   property-decision-checklist   /property lead magnet
#   ai-readiness-scorecard        /business-ai lead magnet
#   wellness-planner              /wellness lead magnet
# ALEESA_API_URL=https://api.aleesa.ai
# ALEESA_WEBSITE_FORM_API_KEY=wform_...

# ---- Optional: also POST leads to a CRM or automation tool ----------
# Fire-and-forget, in addition to Aleesa above. Safe to leave unset.
# LEADS_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.example.com/nabil-leads
# LEADS_WEBHOOK_SECRET=    # sent as: Authorization: Bearer <secret>

# ---- Chat assistant: Anthropic (fallback) ---------------------------
# Used only when the two ALEESA_ variables at the top are unset. The bot is
# then trained by the system prompt in src/lib/chat/anthropic-provider.ts —
# that file is the knowledge base, so edit it to retrain the bot. Nothing is
# stored and no conversation reaches a human.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
